I found the current version of Clinical Coverage Policy 10A and identified a specific section titled **3.2.1.6 Treatment Plan (Plan of Care)**, plus documentation sections that may add requirements. Next I’m reading those full sections and checking whether Policy 10A has any amendments.The plan-of-care section gives a concrete checklist of what the treatment plan must contain, and the documentation section confirms that a copy of the treatment plan must be kept in the record. I’m pulling one nearby section on ordering requirements so I can state the plan-of-care rule in the right context.## Treatment plan / plan of care requirement under NC Medicaid Policy 10A

Under **Clinical Coverage Policy 10A, Section 3.2.1.6 — “Treatment Plan (Plan of Care)”** ([Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)), the outpatient therapy **treatment plan must include**:

- the **duration** of the therapy treatment plan, including **start and end dates**, with a duration of **no more than six months**;
- the **discipline-specific treatment diagnosis** and any **related medical diagnoses**;
- the beneficiary’s **rehabilitative or habilitative potential**;
- **defined goals** for each therapeutic discipline that are **specific and measurable** and have a **reasonable expectation of being achieved within the duration of the therapy plan**;
- the **skilled interventions, methodology, procedures, and specific programs** to be used;
- the **frequency of services**;
- the **length of each treatment visit in minutes**; and
- the **name, credentials, and signature** of the professional completing the treatment plan, **dated on or before the treatment plan start date**.

### Related documentation requirement
Policy 10A also requires that the provider’s records include **“a copy of the treatment plan.”** See **Clinical Coverage Policy 10A, Section 7.2 — “Documenting Services”** ([Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)).

That same documentation section also requires the record to include, among other things:

- the beneficiary’s **name and identification number**;
- **a copy of the order for OST services**;
- a note for each billed date of service describing the **skilled intervention, outcome, beneficiary response, and date of service**;
- the **duration of service in minutes** for each billed date of service;
- the **signature and credentials** of the person providing each service;
- testing documentation or a summary of results, when applicable; and
- other records necessary to disclose the nature and extent of services billed to Medicaid.

### Bottom line
For outpatient therapy under Policy 10A, the plan of care is not just a general narrative. It must be a **signed, dated, time-limited written treatment plan** with diagnoses, prognosis/potential, measurable goals, interventions, frequency, and visit length, and it must be kept in the beneficiary’s record.

**Authority:**  
- **Clinical Coverage Policy 10A, Section 3.2.1.6 — “Treatment Plan (Plan of Care)”** (effective Feb. 1, 2025) ([Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment))  
- **Clinical Coverage Policy 10A, Section 7.2 — “Documenting Services”** (effective Feb. 1, 2025) ([Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment))

